econnection rounds, changes the leader so that the new leader's own recorded value is inflated too, and then calls the public trim(None) on that leader, wrapping the call so a panic is reported as an event field rather than aborting the run.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Entry type Value has Snapshot = NoSnapshot; ClusterConfig { configuration_id: 1, nodes: [1,2,3], flexible_quorum: None } with default ServerConfig (batch_size 1).\", \"Three reconnection rounds of node 1 and node 2 are followed by node 2 taking the lead with try_become_leader(), which in this harness inflates the new leader's own recorded accepted index as witnessed by the staleleader stage.\", \"trim is called with None, which the documentation describes as using the highest trimmable index; the call is wrapped in catch_unwind so a panic becomes a reported outcome.\"], \"excluded\": [\"Snapshots are not exercised; no entry type with use_snapshots() true is used in this case.\", \"No crate or package test suite is executed; only the generated test file.\"], \"parameters\": {\"nodes\": 3, \"entries_before_stopsign\": 5, \"drift_rounds\": 3}}\nprefix = \"Same prefix as the lineage (node 3 leads, five entries decided, StopSign decided). The new case then performs three rounds of node1.reconnected(3)+node2.reconnected(3) with the queue drained each time, calls node2.try_become_leader() and drains again, samples all three nodes as DRIFTTRIM_BEFORE, calls node2.trim(None) inside catch_unwind and emits DRIFTTRIM_TRIM with trim_outcome (ok/err/panic), compacted_idx, accepted_idx and decided_idx of the leader, then samples all three nodes as DRIFTTRIM_AFTER.\"\nrequirement = null\nresponsibility = \"\"\ncomparisons = [{\"event\": \"DRIFTTRIM_BEFORE\", \"identity_fields\": [\"node\"], \"admission_alias\": \"drift_rounds\", \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"accepted_idx\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": 6, \"reference\": null}, \"antecedent\": null, \"applicability_conditions\": [{\"field\": \"node\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": 2, \"reference\": null}], \"description\": \"Baseline of the drift-then-trim case: before the trim the leader still reports six indices of content.\"}, {\"event\": \"DRIFTTRIM_BEFORE\", \"identity_fields\": [\"node\"], \"admission_alias\": \"drift_rounds\", \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"accepted_idx\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": 6, \"reference\": null}, \"antecedent\": null, \"applicability_conditions\": [{\"field\": \"node\", \"op\": \"ne\", \"value\": 2, \"reference\": null}], \"description\": \"Baseline: before the trim the followers still report six indices of content.\"}, {\"event\": \"DRIFTTRIM_TRIM\", \"identity_fields\": [\"node\"], \"admission_alias\": \"drift_before\", \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"trim_outcome\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": \"ok\", \"reference\": null}, \"antecedent\": null, \"applicability_conditions\": [], \"description\": \"The documented trim path succeeds for a leader whose configuration has decided six indices: trim(None) reports no error.\"}, {\"event\": \"DRIFTTRIM_TRIM\", \"identity_fields\": [\"node\"], \"admission_alias\": \"drift_before\", \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"compacted_idx\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": 6, \"reference\": null}, \"antecedent\": null, \"applicability_conditions\": [], \"description\": \"The configuration's decided prefix reaches the compacted index: trim(None) compacts up to the six indices every node decided.\"}, {\"event\": \"DRIFTTRIM_AFTER\", \"identity_fields\": [\"node\"], \"admission_alias\": \"drift_before\", \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"decided_eq_accepted\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": true, \"reference\": null}, \"antecedent\": null, \"applicability_conditions\": [{\"field\": \"node\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": 2, \"reference\": null}], \"description\": \"After the trim the leader's decided index is still covered by the entries it holds.\"}]\nknowledge = []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
